 "provenance": "Item.Recover from the client's own table/Item. Recover = [currencyType, amount]: decomposing one of the item pays `amount` of the currency whose table/CurrencyType TpyeId == currencyType, and that row's ItemID is the bag item that lands (904 = E_BaoShi -> 1237904 宝石碎片, 905 = E_BaoShiJi -> 1237905 宝石姬碎片). It is the rate behind the 背包-分解 page, and the client draws its preview straight from this column: BagDecomposePage_RefreshCurrency (0x19A6354) reads Item+0x78, takes [0] as the currency type and [1] as the per-item amount, and multiplies by the count the player entered, so the server has to settle from the identical column. The curated economy_catalog carries this column only for the rows it lists (just 1250011 among the gems); reward_items.json has no Recover column at all, so the whole column is exported here. Equipment rows carry [906, 1] too, but they are reclaimed through C2L_EquipReclaim instead."
